{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-d27e026afca0066d2e91","statement":"There is a natural equivalence of $\\La$-linear monoidal categories\n\n\\[\n\\Ch\\colon \\indcoh (R_{I_F^t,\\hat{H}})\\cong \\shv_\\mon(H),\n\\]\n\nwhich is $t$-exact with respect to the standard $t$-structures on the source and target. In particular, the monoidal unit $\\cohdual_{R_{I_F^t,\\hat{H}}}$ of $\\indcoh (R_{I_F^t,\\hat{H}})$ corresponds to the monoidal unit $\\widetilde{\\Ch}=\\Ch_\\mon$ of $\\shv_\\mon(H)$.\n\nLet $f: H_1\\to H_2$ be a homomorphism of tori. Under the above equivalences, the adjoint functors $(f^*, f_*^{\\mon})$ from <<ref:lem: functoriality depth zero geom Langlands for tori>> corresponds to the adjoint functor $(\\hat{f}^{\\indcoh}_*,\\hat{f}^{\\indcoh,!})$ between ind-coherent sheaves.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"ec3af715d484dfa4a85326c094ed14ef171176fe886c2e4adad2056803175fc8","kind":"proposition","label":"Proposition 255","ref_key":"lem: depth zero geom Langlands for tori","name":"","order":355,"deps":[{"ref":"lem: functoriality depth zero geom Langlands for tori","card_id":"ma-c-766cd1644d24323fd8d5","label":"Proposition 238","resolved":true,"target":"card"}],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":7593,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":691,"math_hints":56}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspondence","abstract":"In one of our previous articles, we outlined the formulation of a version of the categorical arithmetic local Langlands conjecture. The aims of this article are threefold. First, we provide a detailed account of one component of this conjecture: the local Langlands category. Second, we aim to prove this conjecture in the tame case for quasi-split unramified reductive groups. Finally, we will explore the first applications of such categorical equivalence.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2025","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakb":"{\\mathfrak b}","frakc":"{\\mathfrak c}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakh":"{\\mathfrak h}","frakm":"{\\mathfrak m}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","fraks":"{\\mathfrak s}","frakt":"{\\mathfrak t}","fraku":"{\\mathfrak u}","frakA":"{\\mathfrak A}","frakC":"{\\mathfrak C}","frakM":"{\\mathfrak M}","frakX":"{\\mathfrak X}","bA":"{\\mathbb A}","bB":"{\\mathbb B}","bC":"{\\mathbb C}","bD":"{\\mathbb D}","bF":"{\\mathbb F}","bG":"{\\mathbb G}","bL":"{\\mathbb L}","bN":"{\\mathbb N}","bO":"{\\mathbb O}","bP":"{\\mathbb P}","bQ":"{\\mathbb Q}","bR":"{\\mathbb R}","bT":"{\\mathbb T}","bX":"{\\mathbb X}","bZ":"{\\mathbb Z}","bfA":"{\\mathbf A}","bfB":"{\\mathbf B}","bfC":"{\\mathbf C}","bfD":"{\\mathbf D}","bfE":"{\\mathbf E}","bfF":"{\\mathbf F}","bfG":"{\\mathbf G}","bfH":"{\\mathbf H}","bfI":"{\\mathbf I}","bfK":"{\\mathbf K}","bfL":"{\\mathbf L}","bfM":"{\\mathbf M}","bfN":"{\\mathbf N}","bfP":"{\\mathbf P}","bfR":"{\\mathbf R}","bfS":"{\\mathbf S}","bfT":"{\\mathbf T}","bfa":"{\\mathbf a}","bff":"{\\mathbf f}","mA":"{\\mathcal A}","mB":"{\\mathcal B}","mE":"{\\mathcal E}","mF":"{\\mathcal F}","mG":"{\\mathcal G}","mH":"{\\mathcal H}","mI":"{\\mathcal I}","mJ":"{\\mathcal J}","mK":"{\\mathcal K}","mL":"{\\mathcal L}","mM":"{\\mathcal M}","mN":"{\\mathcal N}","mO":"{\\mathcal O}","mP":"{\\mathcal P}","mQ":"{\\mathcal Q}","mS":"{\\mathcal S}","mT":"{\\mathcal T}","mU":"{\\mathcal U}","mV":"{\\mathcal V}","mW":"{\\mathcal W}","mX":"{\\mathcal X}","mZ":"{\\mathcal Z}","scrA":"{\\mathscr A}","scrB":"{\\mathscr B}","scrS":"{\\mathscr S}","al":"{\\alpha}","ga":"{\\g